  "worked_solution": "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8}-(y+1)^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8}-(0+1)^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8}-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8} & =2 \\\\ (x+2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ x+2 & =\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =-2\\pm 4 \\\\ x & =-6,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are $(-6,0)$ and $(2,0).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
